@startuml Feature7_Seq_2
skinparam maxMessageSize 150
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam roundcorner 5
skinparam minClassWidth 100

title **Feature 7: Department Management - Sequence: Assign Manager**

actor Admin
participant "Web UI" as UI
participant "<<controller>>\nDepartmentController" as Ctrl
participant "<<service>>\nDepartmentService" as Svc
participant "<<repository>>\nUserRepository" as UserRepo
participant "<<repository>>\nDepartmentRepository" as Repo
participant "<<dbcontext>>\nAppDbContext" as DbContext
participant "Database" as DB

Admin -> UI: Select Manager & Update Dept
activate UI

UI -> Ctrl: PUT /api/departments/{id}
activate Ctrl

Ctrl -> Svc: UpdateAsync(companyId, deptId, dto)
activate Svc

Svc -> Repo: GetByIdAsync(companyId, deptId)
activate Repo
Repo --> Svc: return Department entity
deactivate Repo

Svc -> UserRepo: GetByIdAsync(companyId, dto.ManagerUserId)
activate UserRepo
UserRepo --> Svc: return User entity
deactivate UserRepo

note right of Svc: Validate User Status == Active\nand Role == DepartmentManager

Svc -> Repo: SaveAsync()
activate Repo
Repo -> DbContext: Attach & SaveChanges
activate DbContext
DbContext -> DB: Execute SQL UPDATE
activate DB
DB --> DbContext: success
deactivate DB
DbContext --> Repo: success
deactivate DbContext
Repo --> Svc: ok
deactivate Repo

Svc --> Ctrl: return DepartmentDto
deactivate Svc

Ctrl --> UI: return JSON
deactivate Ctrl

UI --> Admin: Show success message
deactivate UI
@enduml
